WEBVTT

00:21.230 --> 00:22.439
Babylon...

00:23.190 --> 00:25.859
Wake up. Wake up.

00:33.909 --> 00:40.207
Please, let me heal Babylon...
let me cast divine sorcery on him!

00:46.004 --> 00:50.092
That's all right.
Go get yourself some rest, miss.

00:50.342 --> 00:53.219
Please! Let me sing!

00:53.220 --> 00:54.595
Get a clue!

00:54.596 --> 00:55.681
Hey!

00:57.432 --> 01:01.562
We were told Babylon was attacked
by someone dressed like a pastor.

01:02.271 --> 01:04.773
We can't trust anyone from the church!

01:33.969 --> 01:37.806
(I Was Reincarnated as the 7th Prince so I Can Take
My Time Perfecting My Magical Ability 2nd Season)

02:54.550 --> 02:58.554
(Episode 18: Escher's Will)

03:10.691 --> 03:12.818
What blasphemy is this?!

03:22.119 --> 03:24.496
I'm... sorry...

03:25.956 --> 03:27.374
Anyone have any ideas?

03:27.749 --> 03:29.626
I'm not sure what you're asking, but...

03:30.252 --> 03:32.712
These are monsters.

03:32.713 --> 03:34.590
There're humans, too.

03:36.675 --> 03:41.305
You can hear what's going on up
in the church pretty clearly.

03:43.182 --> 03:46.058
Considering he mentioned always
hearing Escher's singing,

03:46.059 --> 03:48.520
and his desire to have more security...

03:48.937 --> 03:53.275
I believe this is that man's hideout.

03:53.775 --> 03:58.154
He doesn't seem to be home, though.
Do you think he'll be coming back?

03:58.155 --> 04:02.658
I wouldn't count on it.
Not after the scene he made above.

04:02.659 --> 04:05.871
It's natural to assume this
place would be discovered.

04:06.538 --> 04:09.457
Sylpha! The way these are sewn together,

04:09.458 --> 04:11.876
they look just like the ghouls
we fought in the sewer!

04:11.877 --> 04:13.170
You're right.

04:13.504 --> 04:16.881
Then what happened in the
sewer was a part of it...

04:16.882 --> 04:19.426
But what was he doing down here?

04:20.260 --> 04:21.553
Look at that...

04:22.179 --> 04:23.430
Synthesis.

04:23.805 --> 04:27.433
This place has more of an
alchemical lab than a sorcerous one.

04:27.434 --> 04:30.645
Taking the cells of living organisms
and then cultivating whole limbs,

04:30.646 --> 04:31.939
before attaching them...

04:32.481 --> 04:35.191
It looks like his attempts
to infuse wraiths into people

04:35.192 --> 04:37.736
was a part of that research on synthesis.

04:38.362 --> 04:41.948
All this was going on beneath the church?

04:41.949 --> 04:47.204
This makes it questionable if what we
were fighting were genuine ghouls.

04:47.913 --> 04:50.581
Creatures cobbled together
from various sources...

04:50.582 --> 04:53.168
In other words, chimeras.

04:54.586 --> 04:57.255
This is... horrible!

04:57.256 --> 05:01.343
Toying with lives like this?
He can't get away with it!

05:01.635 --> 05:08.224
The real question being, what did he intend
on doing with the chimeras he was producing?

05:08.225 --> 05:10.810
Well, whatever it is,
it's bound to be nasty.

05:10.811 --> 05:14.481
Yeah. Honestly, it's just so...

05:14.857 --> 05:16.149
Wepugnant!

05:16.358 --> 05:16.859
(Wepugnant?)
(Oh, ho...)

05:17.985 --> 05:19.111
Wepugnant?
(Wepugnant?)

05:19.319 --> 05:21.864
Oh man, this guy sure is awful! Yep!

05:22.406 --> 05:24.448
His sense of ethics might
well be non-existent!

05:24.449 --> 05:27.369
Which makes it likely that he's
modified his own body a lot!

05:27.619 --> 05:32.623
I want to see it. I'd wager his own
body is the culmination of all his study!

05:32.624 --> 05:35.668
Let's destroy this laboratory.

05:35.669 --> 05:37.004
Damn right.

05:38.213 --> 05:39.506
This place is a nightmare!

05:39.798 --> 05:42.008
You're really gonna wreck it? All of it?

05:42.009 --> 05:46.513
After a thorough search so we can inform
Prince Albert of the details, of course.

05:46.889 --> 05:50.767
I'm surprised to learn you know so much
about alchemy as well, Prince Lloyd.

05:51.268 --> 05:54.312
Nah! I just... read about it once...

05:54.313 --> 05:55.522
(Slither...)
Nah! I just... read about it once...

05:59.026 --> 05:59.233
Drop!

05:59.234 --> 06:00.276
(Drop)
Drop!

06:00.277 --> 06:00.903
(Drop)

06:10.704 --> 06:12.622
Is that a lamia?!

06:12.623 --> 06:15.667
The bastard has monsters wandering
loose in this place?!

06:18.212 --> 06:19.796
A... monster?

06:23.050 --> 06:24.092
Don't kill her.

06:30.807 --> 06:33.810
That's the Air-class spell, Ventercier.

06:34.228 --> 06:35.311
Galilea.

06:35.312 --> 06:36.063
On it.

06:36.396 --> 06:37.689
Arachnid Cocoon!

06:38.565 --> 06:39.566
Swerve!
(Swerve)

06:40.692 --> 06:41.901
Go, Ren.

06:41.902 --> 06:42.444
Okay.

06:47.407 --> 06:50.409
A magic barrier? She can use
that kind of technique?

06:50.410 --> 06:52.703
This is gonna take a while.

06:52.704 --> 06:53.705
No.

06:55.207 --> 06:57.835
Kneel! Kneel!

06:59.753 --> 07:01.755
He got the demons with this one.

07:02.881 --> 07:05.592
Mana focus... Recitation Loop!

07:06.718 --> 07:08.846
Kneel! Kneel! Kneel!

07:14.268 --> 07:15.394
Wow!

07:19.147 --> 07:21.108
With a single attack...

07:21.316 --> 07:24.110
With a power like that,
I'm glad you're on our side.

07:24.111 --> 07:26.153
Your cursed speech has gotten way stronger
since you've gained control over it, Crow.

07:26.154 --> 07:27.905
(You used me as a decoy, didn't you?)
Your cursed speech has gotten way stronger since you've gained control over it, Crow.

07:27.906 --> 07:29.116
(Sorry)
Your cursed speech has gotten way stronger since you've gained control over it, Crow.

07:29.366 --> 07:32.244
Now, take a closer look.
It's just like I thought.

07:32.619 --> 07:36.540
She wasn't cultivated in here.
She's human.

07:37.583 --> 07:39.543
Even if half of her is a monster.

07:40.210 --> 07:43.005
Synthesis experiments on living humans?

07:43.255 --> 07:44.923
Who's this guy think he is?!

07:45.465 --> 07:52.222
What do we do? What can we do for her?

07:56.435 --> 07:57.226
Kneel...

07:57.227 --> 07:58.020
Wait!

08:01.106 --> 08:02.566
Please, wait!

08:03.650 --> 08:07.029
It's okay. You don't have to be afraid.

08:07.613 --> 08:09.531
We're all here to help.

08:09.865 --> 08:12.534
Escher, watch out! If you get too close—

08:18.916 --> 08:19.917
Escher!

08:21.710 --> 08:23.545
That makes sense.

08:24.338 --> 08:25.672
I'm sorry.

08:28.759 --> 08:31.428
It's only natural you'd be scared.

08:31.929 --> 08:35.849
I've been scared out of
my mind this whole time.

08:36.308 --> 08:37.726
And feeling powerless.

08:38.310 --> 08:43.732
What can someone like me... even do?

09:10.175 --> 09:12.261
This melody...

09:34.408 --> 09:35.242
Hey.

09:36.410 --> 09:39.288
How long has she been singing?

09:40.080 --> 09:43.667
The entire time.
It's been over twelve hours.

09:44.751 --> 09:46.503
That's crazy!

09:46.920 --> 09:50.340
She isn't even casting divine sorcery!

09:51.008 --> 09:53.676
She's run through all of her mana already!

09:53.677 --> 09:58.515
So how is she still upright?
Still singing?

09:58.849 --> 09:59.808
This girl...

10:00.601 --> 10:04.062
She's amazing.

10:04.897 --> 10:06.815
And her singing...

10:19.077 --> 10:23.372
I remember.
I could hear it all the time...

10:23.373 --> 10:24.708
This singing.

10:26.210 --> 10:29.045
Coming down from that
pitch black ceiling...

10:29.046 --> 10:30.380
The same song.

10:31.590 --> 10:36.595
Even he would stop moving
when he heard it.

10:37.846 --> 10:38.972
I remember.

10:39.389 --> 10:42.893
When it felt like the monster was
going to take over my mind...

10:43.310 --> 10:45.145
I would hear this.

10:45.812 --> 10:49.149
The voice of the person who
kept me from losing myself...

10:54.446 --> 10:56.114
I'm sorry.

10:57.491 --> 11:00.160
Um, I...

11:02.371 --> 11:03.830
I'm...

11:04.915 --> 11:08.752
I'm human! I'm sorry!

11:16.802 --> 11:19.763
I'm sorry, too.

11:20.597 --> 11:23.100
You were so close by...

11:24.977 --> 11:27.437
but I never noticed.

11:45.122 --> 11:47.958
(I Was Reincarnated as the 7th Prince so I Can Take
My Time Perfecting My Magical Ability 2nd Season)

11:48.292 --> 11:51.211
Prince Albert's here!

11:51.670 --> 11:54.715
A chimera laboratory beneath the church.

11:55.048 --> 11:59.428
As much as I'd like to hunt down
the culprit as soon as possible...

12:00.220 --> 12:03.515
I'm sorry I couldn't be of more help.

12:03.849 --> 12:07.227
Amnesia bad enough to make
you forget your own name...

12:07.811 --> 12:10.229
That sounds like a side-effect of
the chimerazation experiments.

12:10.230 --> 12:14.400
I've got a good idea, though.
You probably used to be an adventurer!

12:14.401 --> 12:17.236
That makes sense,
since she could use sorcery.

12:17.237 --> 12:19.572
But even if I knew my identity,

12:19.573 --> 12:22.492
with my body like this, living a normal
life is out of the question...

12:22.868 --> 12:28.706
Relax! We're from Lordost Island, and it's a
place where folks like you can live happy lives.

12:28.707 --> 12:29.916
Come on down!

12:29.917 --> 12:31.751
We'll make a long skirt for you!

12:31.752 --> 12:33.337
Everyone...

12:35.005 --> 12:39.009
Just who exactly is this
mysterious pastor, though?

12:39.259 --> 12:42.762
Oh, I found this in the laboratory.

12:42.763 --> 12:45.390
Do you think it'll be any help?

12:45.933 --> 12:48.519
That's certainly an old-looking rosary.

12:48.894 --> 12:52.980
I'm not sure it belongs to the person
you called the mysterious pastor,

12:52.981 --> 12:55.149
but I do have faint memories of him.

12:55.150 --> 12:58.278
I think he... hates the gods.

12:59.905 --> 13:04.034
I've got something for you,
while we're on the subject.

13:05.744 --> 13:08.538
Those are the notes from the lab...

13:08.539 --> 13:10.456
With the research data!

13:10.457 --> 13:14.044
He snatched them the second he heard
the lab was going to be destroyed.

13:14.461 --> 13:18.048
Lloyd, you can't! Having her look
through this sort of thing...

13:18.257 --> 13:20.801
She can always burn it, if she wants to.

13:22.094 --> 13:26.807
But this data is the only lead we have
in turning you fully human again.

13:27.432 --> 13:30.601
Your body is functioning
thanks to a combination

13:30.602 --> 13:34.272
of mana signatures too complex for
even me to grasp at a glance.

13:34.273 --> 13:37.358
You're the only one
who can learn this data,

13:37.359 --> 13:40.820
compare it to your situation, and figure
out how to change your body back.

13:40.821 --> 13:42.989
Dispose of it, and put it behind you,

13:42.990 --> 13:45.701
or push forward, without looking
away from your trauma.

13:46.076 --> 13:47.411
It's your choice.

13:53.750 --> 13:57.963
Thank you! I'll do what I can!

14:05.596 --> 14:08.848
All right, and we'll help however we can.

14:08.849 --> 14:11.475
And that being the case,
let's give you a name.

14:11.476 --> 14:12.101
(Please enter a name.)
(It can't be changed later.) (Name)

14:12.102 --> 14:15.646
Make it something auspicious sounding, Prince Lloyd!
(Please enter a name.) (It can't be changed later.) (Name)

14:15.647 --> 14:17.064
P-Please. (Please enter a name.)
(It can't be changed later.) (Name)

14:17.065 --> 14:21.236
A name full of hope that she'll be human again someday!
(Please enter a name.) (It can't be changed later.) (Name)

14:21.904 --> 14:23.237
Then...

14:23.238 --> 14:23.779
How about Lami?
Because it sounds like lamia.

14:23.780 --> 14:26.449
(Lami)
How about Lami? Because it sounds like lamia.

14:26.450 --> 14:27.367
(Lami)

14:28.327 --> 14:31.621
Did she go back to the castle already?

14:31.622 --> 14:34.540
Saria... Saria!

14:34.541 --> 14:36.126
Saria!

14:36.418 --> 14:37.377
What?

14:37.669 --> 14:41.256
Saria?! What are you still
doing at the church?

14:41.507 --> 14:44.175
I was eating some of Macaron's babylons.

14:44.176 --> 14:46.512
As a break from my recital practice.

14:48.263 --> 14:51.266
Would you like some, Escher?
Some of Babylon's macarons.

14:52.768 --> 14:54.603
I'm sorry, Saria.

14:55.312 --> 14:58.565
Babylon... I'm going to sing after all.

14:59.233 --> 15:00.901
I want to!

15:01.443 --> 15:05.531
Because it's the only thing I'm good at!

15:06.031 --> 15:08.992
Very good. Let's make it a big show.

15:10.410 --> 15:12.204
For the Great Advent Festival...

15:13.038 --> 15:13.996
(Tousle Tousle)

15:13.997 --> 15:15.540
The Advent Festival must be canceled.
(Tousle Tousle)

15:15.541 --> 15:17.417
The Advent Festival must be canceled.

15:17.918 --> 15:19.168
Whaaat?!

15:19.169 --> 15:20.044
- Good boy.
Whaaat?!

15:20.045 --> 15:24.048
Whaaat?!

15:24.049 --> 15:26.592
Man, the gang's all here now, huh?

15:26.593 --> 15:30.596
Albert, we can't cancel, no matter what!

15:30.597 --> 15:33.475
Well, the thing is, Saria...

15:33.851 --> 15:36.854
I notice she gets his name right.

15:37.145 --> 15:41.190
After what Lami said about the
mysterious pastor having some grudge

15:41.191 --> 15:42.984
against the Church and the gods...

15:42.985 --> 15:43.734
Right!

15:43.735 --> 15:46.238
Everyone, this is incredible!

15:46.488 --> 15:49.157
Look how funny he looks after
I put the necklace on him!

15:49.616 --> 15:51.201
You're right!

15:54.371 --> 15:56.373
It won't come off!

15:57.791 --> 15:58.499
(Bop Bop Bop)

15:58.500 --> 16:05.132
We can assume he hates Escher's singing,
which is to say, hymns.

16:05.465 --> 16:09.343
The real issue is what
exactly he intended to do,

16:09.344 --> 16:11.680
considering the scale of the
laboratory he had built.

16:12.139 --> 16:15.641
I'd probably raise all kinds of
hell at the Great Advent Festival.

16:15.642 --> 16:18.395
I think I'd try and kill the Pope.

16:19.771 --> 16:21.023
Yay!

16:21.481 --> 16:24.859
That sounds really likely...
which means we really ought to cancel...

16:24.860 --> 16:26.736
But how do I make
that kind of announcement?

16:26.737 --> 16:29.531
There's going to be so much backlash,
no matter what I do...

16:30.782 --> 16:33.785
There's an additional
complication to consider.

16:34.119 --> 16:37.663
Regarding the rosary that Lami found...

16:37.664 --> 16:39.290
Wait, where did it go?

16:39.291 --> 16:41.792
Katarina had it a second ago.

16:41.793 --> 16:42.168
(Over here, woof...)

16:42.169 --> 16:43.544
Over here, woof.
(Over here, woof...)

16:43.545 --> 16:43.795
(Over here, woof...)

16:43.921 --> 16:48.049
If this actually did belong
to the mysterious pastor,

16:48.050 --> 16:50.051
things are even worse than we imagined.

16:50.052 --> 16:53.387
I have a silver rosary, too.

16:53.388 --> 16:56.934
It... matches Babylon's.

16:57.267 --> 17:00.437
The one that I saw him with
was practically brand new.

17:01.438 --> 17:03.689
Maybe he needed a new one,
after losing the one she found.

17:03.690 --> 17:06.818
Even if that's the case,
I'm not seeing the problem.

17:07.110 --> 17:09.779
Most rosaries are made from silver.

17:09.780 --> 17:13.115
But this one is solid gold.

17:13.116 --> 17:15.743
Right. A solid gold rosary.

17:15.744 --> 17:19.330
There are only twelve people
allowed to carry those...

17:19.331 --> 17:24.753
Including the Pope, the twelve bishops
who oversee the central church.

17:25.003 --> 17:28.215
You're saying one of the
twelve bishops is the bad guy?!

17:29.007 --> 17:30.675
That's absurd!

17:30.676 --> 17:34.136
These are great holy people,
they would never do such a thing!

17:34.137 --> 17:36.138
- Yeah, that's right...
- For one thing, none of them resemble him!

17:36.139 --> 17:42.896
No. Based on Babylon's description,
he can likely change his form freely.

17:44.273 --> 17:49.360
Th-Then suppose the rosary is a forgery,
or was stolen from one of the bishops...

17:49.361 --> 17:53.407
Whatever the case, there's no way that
one of them could be the culprit!

17:53.657 --> 17:57.160
Oh, Babylon made Escher sad.

17:57.578 --> 18:01.915
You suck! Go get your soul cleansed
with some purification magic.

18:02.249 --> 18:04.376
Then we'll have a nice Babylon!

18:06.211 --> 18:06.294
(Squeak!!!)

18:06.295 --> 18:07.337
Squeak!
(Squeak!!!)

18:07.546 --> 18:09.046
I can sing!

18:09.047 --> 18:12.301
Don't! I don't need purification—

18:13.677 --> 18:14.970
Luxa.

18:16.430 --> 18:21.560
He didn't need a ritual
to use divine sorcery.

18:22.102 --> 18:23.437
He had a pass.

18:26.523 --> 18:28.984
Ever since Prince Lloyd
arranged it for us,

18:29.443 --> 18:31.570
we've been taking it for granted...

18:32.070 --> 18:35.239
Usually, divine sorcery requires a ritual.

18:35.240 --> 18:38.201
Like Escher's singing, or dancing,

18:38.202 --> 18:40.954
which makes it magic that's a bit
more complicated to execute.

18:43.916 --> 18:46.459
That makes it certain, then.

18:46.460 --> 18:51.965
Having a pass that makes divine
sorcery possible without a ritual...

18:56.428 --> 18:59.223
It could only be the 12 bishops.

19:09.399 --> 19:10.983
I found a chess board!

19:10.984 --> 19:12.360
I wanna play!

19:12.361 --> 19:14.987
Hey, I have one of those—

19:14.988 --> 19:16.615
Shut up before you complicate things.

19:18.033 --> 19:19.450
Is that all true?

19:19.451 --> 19:22.620
Broadly, but not quite.

19:22.621 --> 19:26.958
I only gave access to a
pass to the Pope, Guitane.

19:26.959 --> 19:30.420
The other eleven individuals
are people he trusts.

19:31.630 --> 19:35.675
Similar to the relationship between
Prince Lloyd and the Lordost Island people.

19:35.676 --> 19:37.885
I trust you, Prince Lloyd!

19:37.886 --> 19:40.054
I endorse these guys.

19:40.055 --> 19:41.849
Then I trust them too!

19:43.100 --> 19:45.893
Rare to hear you having anything
good to say about a dude...

19:45.894 --> 19:48.647
Then again,
I guess Prince Lloyd is one, too.

19:49.147 --> 19:52.025
And Guitane is a fair comparison.

19:54.903 --> 19:59.198
Given the Church's total rejection
of Babylon's testimony,

19:59.199 --> 20:04.745
I doubt they'll be willing to cancel the
Advent Festival no matter what we tell them.

20:04.746 --> 20:05.621
Oute!

20:05.622 --> 20:07.164
Maybe if we were playing shogi!

20:07.165 --> 20:08.457
And more importantly, if the enemy really
has infiltrated the central church,

20:08.458 --> 20:10.001
Good point...
And more importantly, if the enemy really has infiltrated the central church,

20:10.002 --> 20:10.918
And more importantly, if the enemy really
has infiltrated the central church,

20:10.919 --> 20:15.798
then His Holiness' life would still be in
danger regardless of any cancellation.

20:15.799 --> 20:20.304
True. And most pressingly, there's very
little time left until the festival.

20:24.224 --> 20:28.394
If the mysterious pastor is
among these eleven people...

20:28.395 --> 20:32.273
We'll have to separate the Pope from
his bishops on the day in question,

20:32.274 --> 20:37.070
while we watch them closely,
under the pretext of providing security.

20:40.199 --> 20:43.951
That should at least allow us to
prevent the Pope's assassination

20:43.952 --> 20:46.163
on the day of the Great Advent Festival.

20:46.663 --> 20:49.625
That might be the only
option we really have.

20:50.209 --> 20:52.210
I'll do what I can,

20:52.211 --> 20:55.380
but given the situation,
we can't turn to the Adventurer's Guild.

20:55.797 --> 20:58.217
Those of us here are the only
ones we can really trust.

20:58.675 --> 21:00.927
If you notice anything
suspicious with the bishops,

21:00.928 --> 21:03.137
use your own judgment
to try and secure them.

21:03.138 --> 21:06.183
We need to make sure the Great Advent
Festival ends safely, no matter what!

21:12.272 --> 21:13.148
Wait right there.

21:15.150 --> 21:16.860
Bishop Anastasia.

21:17.736 --> 21:20.321
What's that letter you have there?

21:20.322 --> 21:25.202
Well, it's... a message from
the second prince, Albert.

21:25.661 --> 21:26.953
Let me see it.

21:26.954 --> 21:31.083
But I was told to give it
directly to His Holiness...

21:38.715 --> 21:41.051
B-Bishop Anastasia?

22:03.740 --> 22:07.119
This is a letter sent from the
second prince to the pope.

22:08.453 --> 22:12.331
He wants to inspect
the church's facilities,

22:12.332 --> 22:15.210
with the Pope and the bishops
in separate groups.

22:15.419 --> 22:20.215
I see. Intel gained from the
artificial lamia, I presume.

22:20.465 --> 22:25.554
Yes. It's likely that underground facility
was destroyed by the second prince.

22:25.971 --> 22:30.475
But from the contents of the message,
it seems he didn't learn much—

22:31.935 --> 22:37.065
There was nothing left of Civil War,
apart from this arm.

22:37.608 --> 22:42.278
Granted, his actual cause of death was
the Luma Maxima I provided him with...

22:42.279 --> 22:45.072
But his left arm had already been severed.

22:45.073 --> 22:50.786
It's likely he was engaged in battle with
something even he couldn't react to.

22:50.787 --> 22:53.123
As for what that could be...

22:53.624 --> 22:57.127
I may have overlooked something
rather significant.

22:59.838 --> 23:05.510
However, nothing the second prince
could concoct at this point

23:05.511 --> 23:08.138
should pose any kind of problem.

23:10.766 --> 23:13.809
If he thinks that shutting down
a mere branch laboratory

23:13.810 --> 23:17.271
could impede me even the slightest...

23:17.272 --> 23:21.943
No. Even if he knows exactly
what I intend to do...

23:21.944 --> 23:23.529
it won't matter.

23:27.783 --> 23:30.285
The time has come.

23:32.037 --> 23:38.043
There is no one who can
stop us at this point.

23:41.129 --> 23:42.256
Now...

23:42.714 --> 23:44.341
Let the curtain rise...

23:45.592 --> 23:47.928
on the Great Advent Festival.

23:50.639 --> 23:54.016
The mastermind is among
the twelve bishops?!

23:54.017 --> 23:56.562
My vases... I need to polish
my vases to calm down!

23:57.020 --> 23:59.397
Next time, Episode 19:

23:59.398 --> 24:01.148
"The Great Advent Festival."
(Episode 19 The Great Advent Festival)

24:01.149 --> 24:04.777
You will witness the depths of sorcery.
(Episode 19 The Great Advent Festival)

24:04.778 --> 24:04.987
(Episode 19
The Great Advent Festival)
